  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: bind9.18 security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "description": "Multiple security vulnerabilities have been identified and fixed in BIND 9.18, the DNS server implementation used in Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.6. These include memory exhaustion, denial of service, DNSSEC validation bypass, cache poisoning, assertion failures, and arbitrary code execution issues. The update addresses these issues with security fixes and enhancements, including a new root trust anchor key for DNSSEC.",
